  "articleBody": "Picking out a new lever door handle isn't just about looks – it's about making sure it actually *works* with your door! Before you fall in love with a style, you've got to consider a few practical things. First up, will it fit the existing bore and latch/strike spacing? This is super important because modifying those can be a whole project in itself. You also need to check if the lever is compatible with your door's thickness. Some doors are thinner or thicker than average, and not all levers are universal. Another often-overlooked detail is whether the lockset is designed for a left- or right-handed door, especially for exterior or privacy locks. When you're buying, prioritize the fit specifications and the durability of the mechanism. Make sure the package includes any templates or special mounting hardware you might need. If you're looking to integrate security features or need something specific for a fire-rated door, that's definitely a time to chat with a professional. We can guide you to the perfect, functional fit.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
